---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
---
<Docs slug="cli">
  <h1>CLI</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Drive Ouijit from any terminal it spawns: tasks, hooks, scripts, tags, pull request drafts, themes, and
    panels, all from the shell.
  </p>

  <h2>Where it lives</h2>
  <p>
    The <code>ouijit</code> command is auto-installed into every terminal Ouijit opens, host and sandboxed
    alike. It talks to the running app over a localhost API authenticated by a per-session token, so it only
    works from inside an Ouijit terminal.
  </p>

  <h2>Output format</h2>
  <p>
    Every successful command writes a single JSON value to <code>stdout</code> and exits 0. Errors write
    <code>{`{"error": "..."}`}</code> to <code>stderr</code> and exit non-zero. Pipe to <code>jq</code> to
    extract fields:
  </p>
  <pre class="glass-bevel"><code>ouijit task list | jq '.[] | select(.status == "in_progress") | .name'</code></pre>

  <h2>Project detection</h2>
  <p>
    The CLI detects the active project from your current directory by walking up to the nearest git root. Inside
    a worktree it follows the <code>.git</code> file back to the main repository. Override with
    <code>--project &lt;path&gt;</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Tasks</h2>
  <p>Statuses are <code>todo</code>, <code>in_progress</code>, <code>in_review</code>, and <code>done</code>.</p>
  <pre class="glass-bevel"><code>ouijit task list                              # array of tasks
ouijit task get 5                             # single task
ouijit task current                           # task owning this terminal
ouijit task create "Fix login bug"
ouijit task create "Refactor auth" --prompt "Extract middleware"
ouijit task start 5                           # creates worktree, sets in_progress
ouijit task start 5 --branch custom-name
ouijit task start 5 --run-hook                # run the configured start hook, no dialog
ouijit task start 5 --skip-hook               # spawn the terminal, run no hook
ouijit task start 5 --hook-command "claude"   # one-off command instead of the configured hook
ouijit task start 5 --run-hook --sandbox custom # run it in a sandbox other than the hook's own
ouijit task create-and-start "Add 2FA"        # create + start in one step
ouijit task create-and-start "Add 2FA" --prompt "..." --branch custom --skip-hook
ouijit task spawn "Add 2FA"                   # alias for create-and-start
ouijit task set-status 5 in_review            # the review hook waits behind a pointer by default
ouijit task set-status 5 in_review --run-hook # run the review hook, no dialog
ouijit task set-status 5 in_review --skip-hook
ouijit task set-status 5 done --hook-command "npm run deploy"
ouijit task bulk-set-status done 5 6 7        # set status on many in parallel
ouijit task set-name 5 "Better name"
ouijit task set-description 5 "More detail"
ouijit task set-merge-target 5 develop
ouijit task trash 5                           # worktree goes to the system trash</code></pre>
  <p>
    <code>--run-hook</code>, <code>--skip-hook</code>, and <code>--hook-command</code> are mutually exclusive.
    By default, a status change whose hook would ask first leaves a <a href="#point">pointer</a> at the task, and
    the hook's dialog opens when you follow it, so an agent never puts a dialog over what you're doing. Use these
    flags to run without waiting for you. They apply to <code>task start</code>
    and <code>create-and-start</code> (the start hook) and to <code>set-status</code> into
    <code>in_progress</code>, <code>in_review</code>, or <code>done</code> (the continue, review, and done
    hooks). <code>bulk-set-status</code> takes the same flags. Setting status to <code>todo</code> runs no hook
    and rejects these flags.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>--sandbox host|nono|custom</code> overrides the hook's own <a href="/docs/sandbox/">sandbox</a> setting
    for that run, with or without the flags above. When it waits for you, it is what the dialog preselects.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>ouijit task current</code> resolves the task owning the current terminal via the
    <code>OUIJIT_PTY_ID</code> env var that Ouijit sets on every spawn:
  </p>
  <pre class="glass-bevel"><code>TASK=$(ouijit task current | jq -r .taskNumber)
ouijit task set-status "$TASK" in_review</code></pre>

  <h2>Hooks</h2>
  <p>
    Manage the <a href="/docs/hooks/">lifecycle hooks</a> and the editor command. Hook types are
    <code>start</code>, <code>continue</code>, <code>run</code>, <code>review</code>, <code>done</code>,
    <code>editor</code>.
  </p>
  <pre class="glass-bevel"><code>ouijit hook list
ouijit hook get start
ouijit hook set start --name "Install &amp; agent" --command 'npm install &amp;&amp; claude "$OUIJIT_TASK_DESCRIPTION"'
ouijit hook set run --name "Dev server" --command "npm run dev" --restart-if-running
ouijit hook set continue --name "Agent" --command "claude -c" --sandbox custom
ouijit hook delete done</code></pre>
  <p><code>--restart-if-running</code> applies to the run hook only: relaunch instead of focusing an already-running instance.</p>
  <p>
    <code>--sandbox host|nono|custom</code> applies to the start, continue, review, and done hooks: where the
    hook always runs. <code>nono</code> is Ouijit's sandbox. <code>hook set</code> replaces the whole hook, so leaving it out makes the hook follow the project default.
  </p>

  <h2>Sandbox command</h2>
  <p>
    The launcher for the <a href="/docs/sandbox/#custom">Custom sandbox</a> backend. Host terminals only; a
    sandboxed session gets 403.
  </p>
  <pre class="glass-bevel"><code>ouijit sandbox-command get
ouijit sandbox-command set "$HOME/.local/bin/ouijit-sandbox --strict"
ouijit sandbox-command clear</code></pre>

  <h2>Terminals</h2>
  <p>
    See every open terminal, read what's on its screen, open and close terminals, and paste a message into
    one for you to send. A terminal opened here goes behind the one on screen, and a paste never presses Enter.
    Host terminals only.
  </p>
  <pre class="glass-bevel"><code>ouijit terminal list                          # every project's terminals, with task, sandbox and agent status
ouijit terminal read pty_abc123 --lines 40    # its screen and recent scrollback, as text
ouijit terminal open --task 5                 # a shell in a started task's worktree
ouijit terminal open --task 5 --resume        # running the continue hook
ouijit terminal open                          # a shell in the project
ouijit terminal paste pty_abc123 "run the tests again"
ouijit terminal paste pty_abc123 - &lt; followup.md
ouijit terminal close pty_abc123</code></pre>
  <p>
    A multi-line paste is refused where the program in that terminal would read each newline as Enter.
  </p>

  <h2>Diff notes</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/docs/diff/">notes</a> you've left on a worktree's diff, so an agent can read them itself. Without
    <code>--task</code> it reads the current terminal's worktree, which works from a sandbox too.
  </p>
  <pre class="glass-bevel"><code>ouijit diff notes
ouijit diff notes --task 5
ouijit diff open                              # show this terminal's diff panel
ouijit diff close</code></pre>

  <h2 id="point">Pointing</h2>
  <p>
    An agent can point you at something without moving your screen. A ribbon appears on the thing itself: a
    sidebar row, a board card, a panel tab, a pull request, a line of the diff. Click it, or press
    <kbd>⌘J</kbd> for the latest, to go there. Each terminal has one pointer; a new one replaces it.
  </p>
  <pre class="glass-bevel"><code>ouijit point task 14
ouijit point terminal pty_abc123
ouijit point board
ouijit point pr 212
ouijit point issue ENG-231                    # or a GitHub issue number
ouijit point panel panel-3fa9
ouijit point diff src/auth/session.ts:88
ouijit point note 7f3c                        # from ouijit diff notes
ouijit point clear
ouijit task start 14 --skip-hook --point      # task start, create-and-start and terminal open take --point</code></pre>

  <h2>Tags</h2>
  <p>
    Tag a terminal to <a href="/docs/terminals/">group and filter</a> it. A terminal can carry several, and the pty
    id defaults to the current terminal. Host terminals only; a sandboxed session gets 403.
  </p>
  <pre class="glass-bevel"><code>ouijit tag list                               # tags on open terminals, and which carry each
ouijit tag get                                # this terminal's tags
ouijit tag add review
ouijit tag add review pty_abc123              # explicit pty id
ouijit tag remove review
ouijit tag clear                              # removes all of them</code></pre>

  <h2 id="scripts">Scripts</h2>
  <p>
    Scripts are saved shell commands that show up in the <a href="/docs/panels/">panel menu</a> and the CLI.
    Unlike hooks, they don't fire on lifecycle events.
  </p>
  <pre class="glass-bevel"><code>ouijit script list
ouijit script set --name "Lint" --command "npm run lint"
ouijit script set --name "Dev" --command "npm run dev" --restart-if-running
ouijit script run Lint                        # by name
ouijit script run &lt;id&gt;                        # by id
ouijit script run Tests --task 5              # run inside task 5's worktree
ouijit script delete &lt;id&gt;</code></pre>
  <p>
    <code>script run</code> streams the command's output through your terminal and exits with the command's exit
    code. <code>script set</code> upserts by name, so re-running with the same <code>--name</code> updates that
    script.
  </p>

  <h2>Pull requests</h2>
  <p>
    Inspect <a href="/docs/pull-requests/">pull requests</a> and stage review drafts. Drafts stay local until
    the user sends the review from the app.
  </p>
  <pre class="glass-bevel"><code>ouijit pr list                                # open PRs, grouped review/yours/others
ouijit pr view 42                             # one PR with threads, timeline, checks
ouijit pr link 42 --task 5                    # link a PR to a task
ouijit pr draft list 42
ouijit pr draft add 42 --file src/api.ts --line 88 --body "typo" --origin claude
ouijit pr draft add 42 --file src/api.ts --line 88 --body -   # body from stdin
ouijit pr draft add 42 --file src/api.ts --start-line 80 --line 88 --body "range"
ouijit pr draft discard 42 &lt;draft-id&gt;
ouijit pr lens get 42                         # the lens shown in the Code pane
ouijit pr lens set 42 --body -                # grouping as JSON on stdin
ouijit pr lens clear 42</code></pre>
  <p>
    <code>--body -</code> reads the body from stdin, the safe path for multi-line text. <code>--origin</code>
    names the author shown beside the draft. <code>--side</code> defaults to <code>RIGHT</code> (the new file);
    anchor comments to lines that appear as added lines in the diff.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>pr lens set</code> takes a <a href="/docs/diff/">lens</a> an agent wrote itself: a head sha and the
    parts of the change, each naming paths and new-file line ranges. A range touching any line of a hunk claims
    the whole hunk, so approximate ranges are fine, and omitting a file's ranges claims all of it. Run
    <code>ouijit pr lens set --help</code> for the shape.
  </p>

  <h2>Linear issues</h2>
  <p>
    Read the <a href="/docs/pull-requests/">Linear issues</a> this project is scoped to, link one to a task, and
    stage a comment. Comments stay local until the user sends them from the app, and nothing here moves an
    issue — that is a control on the issue itself.
  </p>
  <pre class="glass-bevel"><code>ouijit linear list                            # this project's issues, in the panel's groups
ouijit linear view ENG-214                    # one issue with its comments and states
ouijit linear link ENG-214 --task 5           # link an issue to a task
ouijit linear draft list ENG-214
ouijit linear draft add ENG-214 --body "the retry loop drops the last error" --origin claude
ouijit linear draft add ENG-214 --body -      # body from stdin
ouijit linear draft discard ENG-214 &lt;draft-id&gt;</code></pre>
  <p>
    A task created from an issue carries its identifier, so
    <code>ouijit task current | jq .linearIssueIdentifier</code> is the issue an agent is working on.
  </p>

  <h2>Markdown panels</h2>
  <p>Open markdown files as <a href="/docs/panels/">panels</a> on a terminal. The pty id defaults to the current terminal.</p>
  <pre class="glass-bevel"><code>ouijit markdown add ./plan.md                 # uses current OUIJIT_PTY_ID
ouijit markdown add ./plan.md pty_abc123      # explicit pty id
ouijit markdown list
ouijit markdown remove ./plan.md</code></pre>

  <h2>Web preview panels</h2>
  <pre class="glass-bevel"><code>ouijit preview add http://localhost:3000      # uses current OUIJIT_PTY_ID
ouijit preview add http://localhost:3000 pty_abc123
ouijit preview list
ouijit preview remove http://localhost:3000</code></pre>

  <h2>Runners</h2>
  <p>
    Run a project <a href="#scripts">script</a> in a <a href="/docs/panels/">runner panel</a> beside a terminal,
    as the <strong>+</strong> menu does, in the project's default sandbox.
  </p>
  <pre class="glass-bevel"><code>ouijit runner add "Dev server"                # by id or name
ouijit runner list
ouijit runner remove "Dev server"             # stops the script</code></pre>

  <h2>Panels</h2>
  <p>Every panel on a terminal, of every kind, and bringing one to the front.</p>
  <pre class="glass-bevel"><code>ouijit panel list                             # ids, kinds, labels, which is active
ouijit panel focus panel-3fa9
ouijit panel focus terminal                   # back to the terminal itself</code></pre>

  <h2>Themes</h2>
  <p><a href="/docs/themes/">Themes</a> are global, not project-scoped.</p>
  <pre class="glass-bevel"><code>{`ouijit theme list                             # preference, presets, custom themes
ouijit theme use dracula
ouijit theme use system
ouijit theme save '{"id":"my-theme","name":"My Theme","base":"dark","tokens":{"--color-accent":"#ff2d55"}}'
ouijit theme save --file my-theme.json
ouijit theme delete my-theme`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Projects</h2>
  <pre class="glass-bevel"><code>ouijit project list                           # every project registered with the app</code></pre>

  <h2 id="environment-variables">Environment variables</h2>
  <p>Ouijit sets these on every terminal it spawns:</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Variable</th><th>What it is</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>OUIJIT_API_URL</code></td><td>Base URL for the local REST API the CLI talks to.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>OUIJIT_API_TOKEN</code></td><td>Bearer token scoped to this terminal session.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>OUIJIT_PTY_ID</code></td><td>Unique id for this terminal session. Used by <code>task current</code> and the panel commands (<code>markdown</code>, <code>preview</code>).</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Hooks get task context on top of these. See <a href="/docs/hooks/#hook-environment">Hooks &rarr; Hook
    environment</a> for the <code>OUIJIT_TASK_*</code> variables.
  </p>
</Docs>
